      { q: "How do I automate futures trading on Rithmic via TradingView?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>You can automate TradingView alerts to <strong>Rithmic</strong> using PickMyTrade as the bridge.</p><p><strong>Step 1: Connect your Rithmic account</strong></p><ul><li>Log in to PickMyTrade</li><li>Go to broker settings and connect your Rithmic account using your credentials</li></ul><p><strong>Step 2: Create your TradingView setup</strong></p><ul><li>Use either a strategy or indicator on TradingView</li><li>Ensure it generates clear buy/sell signals</li></ul><p><strong>Step 3: Create a TradingView alert</strong></p><ul><li>Click \"Create Alert\" on TradingView</li><li>Paste your PickMyTrade webhook URL</li><li>Add your alert message in JSON format (action, symbol, quantity, etc.)</li></ul><p><strong>Step 4: Configure in PickMyTrade</strong></p><ul><li>Map the correct symbol (e.g., MNQ1!, ES1!)</li><li>Set quantity, SL/TP, and other parameters as needed</li></ul><p><strong>Step 5: Test before going live</strong></p><ul><li>Always test using a simulation account</li><li>Check TradingView alert logs and PickMyTrade logs</li></ul><p>You can find detailed step-by-step guides in our documentation: <a href='https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/' target='_blank'>docs.pickmytrade.io/docs</a></p>" },
      { q: "How do I use PickMyTrade with Interactive Brokers (IB)?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>You can automate TradingView alerts with <strong>Interactive Brokers (IB)</strong> using PickMyTrade.</p><p><strong>Step 1: Configure your IB account</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure your IB account is active</li><li>Enable API access in IBKR settings</li><li>Complete the IB connection setup in PickMyTrade</li></ul><p><strong>Step 2: Connect IB to PickMyTrade</strong></p><ul><li>Log in to PickMyTrade</li><li>Add and connect your Interactive Brokers account from the dashboard</li></ul><p><strong>Step 3: Set up TradingView alerts</strong></p><ul><li>Create alerts using your indicator or strategy</li><li>Paste the PickMyTrade webhook URL</li><li>Add alert message in JSON format (action, symbol, quantity, etc.)</li></ul><p><strong>Step 4: Symbol mapping</strong></p><ul><li>Map TradingView symbols correctly to IB contract formats</li><li>This is important for proper order execution</li></ul><p><strong>Step 5: Test your setup</strong></p><ul><li>Start with small size or paper trading</li><li>Verify alerts are received and orders are executed correctly</li></ul><p>You can find detailed step-by-step guides in our documentation: <a href='https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/' target='_blank'>docs.pickmytrade.io/docs</a></p>" },
      { q: "How do I copy trades to multiple prop firm accounts automatically?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Trade copying is a popular feature for prop firm traders managing multiple funded accounts. There are two ways to do this with PickMyTrade:</p><p><strong>1. Using TradingView (Strategy/Indicator automation)</strong></p><ul><li>Connect all your prop firm accounts (Tradovate, Rithmic, ProjectX, etc.) in PickMyTrade</li><li>Create a single TradingView alert for your strategy or indicator</li><li>Send the webhook to PickMyTrade — trades are automatically executed across all connected accounts</li><li>This works for automation across multiple accounts, even across different brokers</li></ul><p><strong>2. Manual trading (Copy trading)</strong></p><ul><li>If you are placing trades manually, you can copy trades between accounts</li><li>Supported combinations: Tradovate → Tradovate, ProjectX → ProjectX, ProjectX → Tradovate</li></ul><p><strong>Key benefits:</strong></p><ul><li>Eliminates manual copying delays</li><li>Ensures consistent entries across accounts</li><li>Reduces execution errors</li><li>Helps scale your strategy across multiple funded accounts</li></ul>" },
      { q: "How do I connect TradingView to TradeStation for automated execution?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>You can automate TradingView alerts to <strong>TradeStation</strong> using PickMyTrade.</p><p><strong>Step 1: Connect your TradeStation account</strong></p><ul><li>Log in to PickMyTrade</li><li>Add and connect your TradeStation account from the dashboard</li></ul><p><strong>Step 2: Create your TradingView setup</strong></p><ul><li>Use a strategy or indicator on TradingView</li><li>Ensure it generates clear buy/sell signals</li></ul><p><strong>Step 3: Create TradingView alerts</strong></p><ul><li>Click \"Create Alert\"</li><li>Paste your PickMyTrade webhook URL</li><li>Add alert message in JSON format (action, symbol, quantity, etc.)</li></ul><p><strong>Step 4: Configure in PickMyTrade</strong></p><ul><li>Map the correct symbols</li><li>Set quantity and other parameters as needed</li></ul><p><strong>Step 5: Test before going live</strong></p><ul><li>Use paper trading or small size first</li><li>Check logs to confirm alerts and executions</li></ul><p>You can find detailed step-by-step guides in our documentation: <a href='https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/' target='_blank'>docs.pickmytrade.io/docs</a></p>" }
