  // ─── 33. TRADOVATE — ADDITIONAL Q&As ───
  {
    category: "Tradovate — Additional Questions",
    icon: "&#8853;",
    description: "Inactivity fees, margin rules, desktop app, contract types, and more",
    questions: [
      { q: "Does Tradovate charge an inactivity fee if I stop trading?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>Yes. On the Free Account Plan, if you log in during a calendar month but place no live trades, Tradovate charges a $35 inactivity fee, and accounts holding funds can also see a separate dormancy charge after a prolonged period without activity. The simplest way to avoid it is to place at least one live trade each month or to keep the account unfunded when you're not trading. Fees change, so confirm the current amounts on Tradovate's official pricing and account-plan pages before relying on them.</p>" },
      { q: "How do I close my Tradovate account, and can my data be deleted?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>To close a Tradovate account, withdraw your full balance and cancel any auto-renewing add-ons or market-data subscriptions; once there's no balance and no active subscription, you won't be charged further and the account simply goes dormant — you can reopen it anytime by logging in and depositing. Full deletion of your personal records isn't possible, because U.S. futures regulations require brokerages to retain customer information for about five years. For help, contact Tradovate support directly.</p>" },
      { q: "What is Tradovate's auto-liquidation policy and when does it trigger?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Tradovate can auto-liquidate your open positions if your account falls below the required margin. Intraday margin applies until about 15 minutes before the session close, at which point the higher initial (overnight) margin is required — if your account can't cover it, the order desk closes your position and emails you a notice. Brokerage margin rules always override any custom risk settings you've configured, so check the live margin schedule on Tradovate's site before holding size into the close.</p>" },
      { q: "What are Tradovate's intraday vs. overnight (initial) margin requirements?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Intraday margins on Tradovate are typically much lower than the exchange's initial (overnight) margin because day trades carry less risk, and they apply from product open until roughly 15 minutes before the session close. Standard intraday rates generally apply up to about 25 mini or 50 micro contracts; beyond that, the requirement steps up (commonly to 50% of initial margin on the excess). Margin numbers vary by product and change with volatility, so always check Tradovate's current margin table for ES, NQ, MES, MNQ and others.</p>" },
      { q: "Are Tradovate's stop-loss and bracket (OCO) orders held on the server or on my computer?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Tradovate's OCO bracket orders (stop loss + profit target) are server-side, meaning they live on Tradovate's infrastructure rather than your local app. If your internet drops or you close the platform, your protective stop and target stay working, and when one fills the other is automatically cancelled. This is why brackets are safe to use on positions you intend to hold, including overnight — though you should still verify your orders are active after any reconnect.</p>" },
      { q: "Is there a Tradovate desktop app, and can I log into web, desktop, and mobile with the same account?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>Yes. Tradovate is cloud-based, so the same username and password work across the downloadable Windows/Mac desktop app, any web browser, and the iOS/Android mobile apps — there's no separate registration per device. The desktop app mirrors the full functionality of the web trader, and your positions and orders sync everywhere because everything runs against the same server-side account. You can grab the desktop installer and mobile apps from Tradovate's official Devices page.</p>" },
      { q: "What is Tradovate's mini-to-micro contract fungibility?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Mini-to-micro fungibility lets you scale a position down to Micro contracts without fully flattening it — for example, instead of closing one E-mini S&amp;P 500 contract, you can convert to its 10 Micro-equivalent and trim exposure gradually. Conversions are based on notional size (1 E-mini = 10 Micros), so you can reduce risk while staying in the trade. It's especially useful for prop traders managing position limits, but the firm must opt in at the vendor level, so confirm availability on your specific account.</p>" },
      { q: "What's the difference between Tradovate's Micro, Mini, and Nano contracts, and which should a beginner trade?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>On Tradovate, E-mini contracts (like ES) are the standard retail size, Micros (MES, MNQ, MYM, M2K) are 1/10 the size of the equivalent mini, and Nano/Event contracts are smaller still — so dollar risk per tick shrinks as you go down the ladder. Most new futures traders start with Micros because they give real market exposure with survivable per-contract risk, often letting you trade with a few hundred to a couple thousand dollars. Always confirm the current contract specs and day-trading margins for each product on Tradovate, since they vary by instrument.</p>" },
      { q: "Do I need a separate Tradovate login for a funded/prop account versus my personal account?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>Yes — a prop-firm Tradovate account is issued and credentialed by the prop firm, so it has its own username/password that you'll find on the firm's dashboard, separate from any personal Tradovate brokerage login. You connect each set of credentials independently, and it's good practice to keep funded-account activity tracked apart from personal trades. PickMyTrade can automate prop-firm Tradovate accounts the same way it automates personal ones, once you've linked the correct credentials.</p>" },
      { q: "Does Tradovate support trailing stops, and are they trailed on the server?", level: "intermediate", a: "<p>Yes. Tradovate offers Trailing Stop and Trailing Stop Limit orders, plus Auto Trail and Auto Breakeven automation, alongside Market, Limit, Stop, Stop Limit, OSO and OCO. Like Tradovate's other bracket orders, these are managed server-side, so the trail keeps adjusting even if your platform disconnects. Behavior can differ slightly between the web, desktop and mobile clients, so test a trailing stop on a sim account first to confirm it trails the way you expect.</p>" },
      { q: "How much does CME real-time market data cost on Tradovate, and can I get it free?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>Tradovate sells the CME Group bundle (CME, CBOT, COMEX, NYMEX) at roughly $12/month for Level 1 or about $41/month for Level 2, with single exchanges available for less; professional traders pay higher exchange-set rates. Importantly, opting into one of Tradovate's paid Account Plans on a funded live account includes free Level 1 CME Group and EUREX data, plus TradingView access, Market Replay and Order Flow+ tools. Data fees are set by the exchanges and change periodically, so verify current rates on Tradovate's market-data page.</p>" },
      { q: "Why are my Tradovate charts showing delayed or no data, and how do I fix it?", level: "beginner", a: "<p>Delayed quotes or 'no data' on Tradovate almost always mean you haven't subscribed to (or activated) the relevant exchange's real-time market data — sim accounts and unsubscribed live accounts default to delayed feeds. Subscribe to the CME bundle or the specific exchange in your account settings, or enroll in an Account Plan that includes free Level 1 CME/EUREX data, then refresh the platform. If data is still missing after subscribing, confirm your non-professional self-certification is on file, since professional status changes data entitlements and pricing.</p>" }
    ]
  }
];

// ===================================================
// RENDER & INTERACTIONS
// ===================================================
document.getElementById('faqStatic').style.display = 'none';

const tocGrid    = document.getElementById('tocGrid');
const faqContent = document.getElementById('faqContent');
const noResults  = document.getElementById('noResults');
const backToTop  = document.getElementById('backToTop');
const searchInput = document.getElementById('searchInput');
const searchCount = document.getElementById('searchCount');
const searchDropdown = document.getElementById('searchDropdown');
const filterPills = document.querySelectorAll('.filter-pill');

const colorMap = {
  beginner    : 'var(--accent-green)',
  intermediate: 'var(--accent-amber)',
  advanced    : 'var(--accent-rose)',
  expert      : 'var(--accent-purple)'
};

// Strip HTML tags for plain-text searching of answer content
const stripHtml = html => html.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ');

// Collect refs so search/filter can show/hide elements without re-rendering
const categoryRefs = [];
let totalQuestions = 0;

FAQ_DATA.forEach((cat, catIndex) => {
  const tocCard = document.createElement('a');
  tocCard.className = 'toc-card';
  tocCard.href = '#cat-' + catIndex;
  tocCard.setAttribute('role', 'listitem');
  tocCard.setAttribute('aria-label', `${cat.category} — ${cat.questions.length} questions`);
  tocCard.innerHTML = `
    <div class="toc-num">${catIndex + 1}</div>
    <div class="toc-card-body">
      <div class="toc-cat-name">${cat.category}</div>
      <div class="toc-cat-count">${cat.questions.length} questions</div>
    </div>`;
  tocCard.addEventListener('click', e => {
    e.preventDefault();
    document.getElementById('cat-' + catIndex)?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
  });
  tocGrid.appendChild(tocCard);

  const section = document.createElement('section');
  section.className = 'cat-section';
  section.id = 'cat-' + catIndex;
  section.innerHTML = `
    <div class="cat-section-header">
      <div class="cat-section-title">${cat.icon} ${catIndex + 1}. ${cat.category}</div>
      <hr class="cat-section-hr" />
    </div>`;

  const itemRefs = [];
  cat.questions.forEach(item => {
    const faqItem = document.createElement('div');
    faqItem.className = 'gfaq-item';
    faqItem.dataset.level = item.level;
    faqItem.dataset.cat   = catIndex;
    faqItem.innerHTML = `
      <button class="gfaq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="diff-dot" style="background:${colorMap[item.level] || 'var(--text-muted)'}" title="${item.level}"></span>
        <span class="q-text">${item.q}</span>
        <span class="gfaq-toggle">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="gfaq-answer"><div class="gfaq-answer-inner">${item.a}</div></div>`;

    const btn = faqItem.querySelector('.gfaq-btn');
    const toggle = faqItem.querySelector('.gfaq-toggle');
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const isOpen = faqItem.classList.contains('open');
      if (!isOpen) {
        faqItem.classList.add('open');
        const ans = faqItem.querySelector('.gfaq-answer');
        ans.style.maxHeight = ans.scrollHeight + 'px';
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        toggle.textContent = '×';
      } else {
        faqItem.classList.remove('open');
        faqItem.querySelector('.gfaq-answer').style.maxHeight = null;
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        toggle.textContent = '+';
      }
    });

    section.appendChild(faqItem);
    itemRefs.push({
      el: faqItem,
      level: item.level,
      q: item.q,
      catName: cat.category,
      catIndex: catIndex,
      haystack: (item.q + ' ' + stripHtml(item.a) + ' ' + cat.category).toLowerCase()
    });
    totalQuestions++;
  });

  faqContent.appendChild(section);
  categoryRefs.push({ tocCard, section, items: itemRefs, total: cat.questions.length });
});

// ─── DIFFICULTY FILTER (search does NOT filter — see dropdown below) ─────
let activeLevel = 'all';

function applyFilter() {
  let totalVisible = 0;

  categoryRefs.forEach(({ tocCard, section, items, total }) => {
    let visible = 0;
    items.forEach(({ el, level }) => {
      const show = activeLevel === 'all' || level === activeLevel;
      el.style.display = show ? '' : 'none';
      if (!show && el.classList.contains('open')) {
        el.classList.remove('open');
        const ans = el.querySelector('.gfaq-answer');
        if (ans) ans.style.maxHeight = null;
        const tg = el.querySelector('.gfaq-toggle');
        if (tg) tg.textContent = '+';
        const btn = el.querySelector('.gfaq-btn');
        if (btn) btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      }
      if (show) visible++;
    });

    section.style.display = visible > 0 ? '' : 'none';
    tocCard.style.display = visible > 0 ? '' : 'none';
    const countEl = tocCard.querySelector('.toc-cat-count');
    if (countEl) {
      countEl.textContent = activeLevel !== 'all'
        ? `${visible} match${visible === 1 ? '' : 'es'}`
        : `${total} questions`;
    }
    totalVisible += visible;
  });

  noResults.classList.toggle('visible', totalVisible === 0);

  searchCount.innerHTML = activeLevel !== 'all'
    ? `Showing <strong>${totalVisible}</strong> of <strong>${totalQuestions}</strong> questions`
    : '';
}

// ─── DROPDOWN: live search results with click-to-jump ───────────
const allItems = categoryRefs.flatMap(c => c.items);
const MAX_DROPDOWN_RESULTS = 10;
let dropdownActiveIndex = -1;

function escapeHtml(s) {
  return s.replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
}

function highlightMatch(text, query) {
  const escaped = escapeHtml(text);
  if (!query) return escaped;
  const re = new RegExp('(' + query.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&') + ')', 'ig');
  return escaped.replace(re, '<mark>$1</mark>');
}

function renderDropdown(query) {
  if (!query) {
    closeDropdown();
    return;
  }

  const matches = [];
  for (const item of allItems) {
    if (item.haystack.includes(query)) {
      matches.push(item);
      if (matches.length >= MAX_DROPDOWN_RESULTS) break;
    }
  }

  searchDropdown.innerHTML = '';
  dropdownActiveIndex = -1;

  if (matches.length === 0) {
    searchDropdown.innerHTML = `<div class="search-empty">No matches for "${escapeHtml(query)}"</div>`;
  } else {
    matches.forEach((item, i) => {
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'search-result';
      row.setAttribute('role', 'option');
      row.setAttribute('id', 'searchResult-' + i);
      row.dataset.index = i;
      row.innerHTML = `
        <span class="res-dot" style="background:${colorMap[item.level] || 'var(--text-muted)'}"></span>
        <div class="res-body">
          <div class="res-q">${highlightMatch(item.q, query)}</div>
          <div class="res-cat"><i class="fas fa-folder text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>${escapeHtml(item.catName)}</div>
        </div>`;
      row.addEventListener('mousedown', e => {
        e.preventDefault(); // prevent input blur before click fires
        jumpToItem(item);
      });
      row.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => setActiveDropdownRow(i));
      searchDropdown.appendChild(row);
    });

    const hint = document.createElement('div');
    hint.className = 'search-hint';
    hint.innerHTML = `<span><kbd>↑</kbd><kbd>↓</kbd> navigate</span><span><kbd>Enter</kbd> open</span><span><kbd>Esc</kbd> close</span>`;
    searchDropdown.appendChild(hint);
  }

  searchDropdown.classList.add('visible');
  searchInput.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
}

function closeDropdown() {
  searchDropdown.classList.remove('visible');
  searchDropdown.innerHTML = '';
  searchInput.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
  searchInput.removeAttribute('aria-activedescendant');
  dropdownActiveIndex = -1;
}

function setActiveDropdownRow(index) {
  const rows = searchDropdown.querySelectorAll('.search-result');
  if (rows.length === 0) return;
  if (index < 0) index = rows.length - 1;
  if (index >= rows.length) index = 0;
  rows.forEach(r => r.classList.remove('active'));
  rows[index].classList.add('active');
  rows[index].scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });
  dropdownActiveIndex = index;
  searchInput.setAttribute('aria-activedescendant', rows[index].id);
}

function jumpToItem(item) {
  closeDropdown();
  // Make sure the target is visible regardless of current filter state
  if (item.el.style.display === 'none') {
    item.el.style.display = '';
    item.catName && (categoryRefs[item.catIndex].section.style.display = '');
  }
  // Smooth-scroll with header offset
  const rect = item.el.getBoundingClientRect();
  const targetY = window.scrollY + rect.top - 90;
  window.scrollTo({ top: targetY, behavior: 'smooth' });
  // Expand the answer
  if (!item.el.classList.contains('open')) {
    const btn = item.el.querySelector('.gfaq-btn');
    if (btn) btn.click();
  }
  // Brief flash highlight
  item.el.classList.remove('flash');
  void item.el.offsetWidth; // restart animation
  item.el.classList.add('flash');
  setTimeout(() => item.el.classList.remove('flash'), 1700);
}

// Debounced input handler — only drives the dropdown, never filters the FAQ
let searchTimer;
searchInput.addEventListener('input', e => {
  clearTimeout(searchTimer);
  searchTimer = setTimeout(() => {
    renderDropdown(e.target.value.trim().toLowerCase());
  }, 120);
});

searchInput.addEventListener('focus', e => {
  const q = searchInput.value.trim().toLowerCase();
  if (q) renderDropdown(q);
});

// Close on outside click
document.addEventListener('click', e => {
  if (!e.target.closest('.search-wrap')) closeDropdown();
});

filterPills.forEach(pill => {
  pill.addEventListener('click', () => {
    filterPills.forEach(p => {
      p.classList.remove('active');
      p.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
    });
    pill.classList.add('active');
    pill.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');
    activeLevel = pill.dataset.level;
    applyFilter();
  });
});

// Keyboard shortcuts: '/' to focus search, arrows + Enter for dropdown, Esc to clear/close
document.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
  const tag = document.activeElement && document.activeElement.tagName;
  const inSearch = document.activeElement === searchInput;
  const dropdownOpen = searchDropdown.classList.contains('visible');

  if (e.key === '/' && tag !== 'INPUT' && tag !== 'TEXTAREA') {
    e.preventDefault();
    searchInput.focus();
    searchInput.select();
  } else if (inSearch && dropdownOpen && (e.key === 'ArrowDown' || e.key === 'ArrowUp')) {
    e.preventDefault();
    setActiveDropdownRow(dropdownActiveIndex + (e.key === 'ArrowDown' ? 1 : -1));
  } else if (inSearch && dropdownOpen && e.key === 'Enter') {
    e.preventDefault();
    const rows = searchDropdown.querySelectorAll('.search-result');
    const idx = dropdownActiveIndex >= 0 ? dropdownActiveIndex : 0;
    if (rows[idx]) {
      const item = allItems[parseInt(rows[idx].dataset.index, 10)];
      if (item) jumpToItem(item);
    }
  } else if (e.key === 'Escape' && inSearch) {
    if (dropdownOpen) {
      closeDropdown();
    } else {
      searchInput.value = '';
      searchInput.blur();
    }
  }
});

window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
  backToTop.classList.toggle('visible', window.scrollY > 500);
}, { passive: true });

backToTop.addEventListener('click', () => {
  window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
});
</script>
</BaseLayout>
